WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
At reception they ask “What is your name?” and Jorge blurts out “From Colombia”—they asked his name, not origin.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Before replying, listen for whether the question carries name, from, or old, and plan a polite closing.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Name calls for “My name is Alex”; from asks origin; and when meeting someone you close with “Nice to meet you”.

4
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Practice: when someone says “Hi, I am Sam”, which reply greets, gives your name, and closes politely?

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Option A is right: it combines greeting, your name, and “Nice to meet you” without mixing origin or farewells.

6
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Use the exact same pattern at a Leeds GP desk or with a new neighbour: greeting, name, and courtesy.
